{
  "_comment": [
    "Accepted duplication. Every entry is a deliberate decision, not a backlog item.",
    "An allowlisted cluster does not fail the duplication check; it appears in the drift",
    "watch instead, with each member's similarity to the family reference.",
    "",
    "A cluster whose files are only PARTLY matched by an entry fails as",
    "'accepted family gained a member'. That is the point: when a plugin joins a family,",
    "its path goes in here in the same change, so the family stays enumerable",
    "(.claude/rules/plugin-authoring.md).",
    "",
    "Do not widen a pattern to silence a finding. Widening is how a new undocumented",
    "clone family becomes invisible.",
    "",
    "decision: D-1  no shared library code between plugins; each is its own Go module.",
    "decision: D-2  the six addon-* plugins are absolute; permanent, never a refactor target.",
    "decision: D-4  cross-module mirrors. src/agent, src/cli and",
    "               src/terraform-provider-mcharbor are separate Go modules and cannot",
    "               import the host, so a shared contract exists as a copy on each side.",
    "",
    "See .references/todo/2026-09-27-deduplication-and-authoring-guardrails.md."
  ],
  "accepted": [
    {
      "family": "agent-protocol-mirror",
      "decision": "D-4",
      "permanent": true,
      "reason": "The agent is a separate Go module and cannot import the host, so the wire protocol exists as a verbatim copy on each side. This is the highest-value drift watch in the repo: if these two disagree, the agent transport breaks in ways no test on either side alone can see. There is no build-time check, only a diff.",
      "patterns": [
        "src/agent/protocol.go",
        "src/backend/core/agent/protocol.go"
      ],
      "baselines": {
        "src/backend/core/agent/protocol.go": {
          "src/agent/protocol.go": 0.9282
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "family": "agent-host-update-script",
      "decision": "D-4",
      "permanent": false,
      "reason": "The host builds the update script and the agent executes it; both modules need the same generator. Separate modules, so a copy each. The one-sided server helpers downloadFailed and skipUnavailableHonoured stay out of the agent on purpose: the single download retry runs inside the generated shell script on both sides, and the server classifies the returned output into the Skip unavailable hint for agent runs too (host_update.go failureHint).",
      "patterns": [
        "src/agent/host_update_script.go",
        "src/agent/host_update_script_test.go",
        "src/backend/modules/system/host_update_script.go",
        "src/backend/modules/system/host_update_script_test.go"
